      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A Stack is a fundamental LIFO (Last-In-First-Out) data structure. Think of it like a stack of plates - you can only add or remove plates from the top. All operations (push, pop, peek) have O(1) time complexity, making stacks extremely efficient. Stacks are used in function call management, expression evaluation, undo mechanisms, and backtracking algorithms."
